Description: docker: parse multi-scope insufficient_scope challenges
 A cross-repo blob mount makes the registry demand a token covering both the
 destination and the source repository, so its WWW-Authenticate: Bearer
 challenge carries a scope with two space-separated tokens, e.g.
 "repository:group/dest:pull,push repository:other/src:pull".
 .
 parseAuthScope split the whole value on ':' and required exactly three
 fields, so any multi-scope challenge failed to parse; the client then never
 re-requested a correctly scoped token and the push failed. parseAuthScopes
 splits on whitespace per the distribution token-auth spec and parses each
 token, and the request path carries the whole set.
 .
 Drop this patch once the forwarded PR lands and reaches the archive: the
 Containerfile stops applying it and the podman suffix goes back to a plain
 rebuild.
 .
 Generated with one line of context on purpose. Three lines pulls in the
 loop header of needsRetryWithUpdatedScope, which trixie spells with
 parseAuthHeader and resolute with iterateAuthHeader; at one line the same
 patch applies to both and there is no per-suite copy to keep in step.
